MECHANISM: how much of sigma* IS the baseline?
================================================================================================
    K   rho(sigma*, dist-NN)   rho(sigma*, #nbrs)   sigma*/sqrt(prior)
   15                +0.6579              -0.7621               0.9909
   30                +0.6610              -0.7433               0.9791
   60                +0.6709              -0.7212               0.9565
  200                +0.7069              -0.6696               0.8849
  500                +0.7504              -0.5964               0.7937
  If sigma* converges on dist-to-NN as the radius tightens, the GP is not
  adding information -- it is recomputing the baseline at the cost of a solve
  per test point. sigma*/sqrt(prior) -> 1 means reversion to the prior.

